# Job-seniority expected-compensation tiers
Workstream-ID: lea-05
GitHub-Issue: https://github.com/Zanark/LinkedIn-EasyApply-Automaton/issues/6
Publication: PUBLIC_SAFE_PROJECTION
Source-record: TODO.md, 2026-07-21 tiered expected-compensation batch
Status: DONE
Milestone: Per-job compensation policy with explicit unknown-tier fallback
Dependencies: lea-04

## Purpose
Choose configured expected compensation according to job seniority without
learning a job-specific result as an applicant-wide answer. Actual tier values
remain private and are absent from this projection.

## Tasks
- [x] Detect three seniority tiers from job titles with experience-level fallback.
- [x] Use the configured lowest-tier fallback when seniority is unknown.
- [x] Set a per-job resolver override and log its decision.
- [x] Keep expected-compensation answers job-specific and out of learned global answers.
- [x] Preserve current-compensation calculation separately.
- [x] Add seniority and resolver coverage; synchronize affected documentation.

## Acceptance criteria
- [x] Historical tests cover title-level distinctions and unknown-title fallback.
- [x] Job-specific expected values cannot become globally learned answers.

## Completion evidence
The 2026-07-21 source records 39 seniority cases, expanded salary/notice tests,
a 163-test green suite, clean Ruff/Black/mypy checks and parsed configuration.
Relevant symbols include `detect_seniority`, `_apply_expected_ctc_tier` and
`set_expected_ctc`. Later explicit monthly overrides are tracked by lea-06.
These are attributed historical results; this migration did not rerun product
tests or establish human acceptance, target qualification or publication.

## Completion log
- 2026-07-21: Tier inference, resolver overrides and local verification recorded complete.
- 2026-11-06: Imported as a public-safe technical workstream without personal amounts.
